---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const description =
  "Draft terms of use for the Straight Up Digital website: what the site is for, the limits of the information published, intellectual property and liability.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
  noindex
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <div class="legal__banner" role="note">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 4v5c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V7l8-4Z"></path><path d="M12 8v4M12 15v.5"></path></svg>
        <p>
          <strong>Draft for review.</strong> These terms are a working draft and
          have not been approved by a lawyer. The legal entity details, liability
          wording and governing-law clause must be confirmed before launch.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="legal__meta">Version terms-draft-2026-11 · Last updated 13 November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          These terms apply to this website. By using it, you agree to them. If you
          do not agree, please stop using the site.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website is operated by <strong>Straight Up Digital</strong>. The
          registered entity name and address are still to be confirmed.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What this website is for</h2>
        <p>
          The site explains the audit and the services offered, and lets you send an
          enquiry. It is an introduction, not a contract. Any work is governed by a
          separate written proposal or agreement, signed before the work starts.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Information is general</h2>
        <p>
          The content is written in good faith and kept as accurate as practical,
          but it is general information. It is not legal, financial, accounting or
          other professional advice, and it should not be relied on as if it were.
        </p>

        <h2>4. No guarantee of results</h2>
        <p>
          The audit is directional. It does not measure traffic, search volume,
          revenue or conversions, and it does not guarantee rankings, enquiries or
          sales. Search results change for reasons outside anyone’s control. Any
          example on this site is labelled as an example and is not client data.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Enquiries and quotes</h2>
        <p>
          Sending the form does not create a contract or oblige either party to
          proceed. A quote is valid for the period stated in it. Work begins only
          after a written scope and quote are accepted.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The brand, logo, text, layout and images on this site belong to Straight
          Up Digital or are used with permission. You may read, print and share
          pages for your own use. You may not copy the site or the brand into
          another product, or suggest that Straight Up Digital endorses it, without
          written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site may link to third-party websites, such as hosting or platform
          documentation. Those sites are not under our control and their terms and
          privacy notices apply.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to keep the site available and correct, but we do not promise
          uninterrupted access. Maintenance, hosting problems or security work may
          take it offline temporarily.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent the law allows, Straight Up Digital is not liable for loss
          caused by relying on general information on this site, by a third-party
          site we link to, or by the site being temporarily unavailable. Nothing in
          these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
        </p>
        <div class="placeholder-note">
          <strong>Lawyer to confirm:</strong> the liability wording and any
          consumer-protection limits that apply.
        </div>

        <h2>10. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Personal information is handled as described in the{" "}
          <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are intended to be governed by South African law. This
          depends on the final legal entity and must be confirmed with the lawyer
          reviewing this draft.
        </p>
        <div class="placeholder-note">
          <strong>Owner and lawyer to confirm:</strong> the legal entity, the
          jurisdiction and the dispute-resolution route.
        </div>

        <h2>12. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change. The version date at the top will change with
          them. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the new
          version.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent through the{" "}
          <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
